{"repositoryId":1177083879,"availability":"available","full":"metalabel/dfos","name":"dfos","description":"Dark Forest OS identity and content protocol, reference implementations, schemas and tests","category":"Other","language":"Go","stars":39,"forks":2,"created":"2026-03-09T17:17:29Z","updated":"2026-10-16T20:23:10Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://protocol.dfos.com","topics":[],"demo":"https://dfos-siwd-demo.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:23.120Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:23.120Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:23.120Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T02:48:13.655Z","stars":39,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-17T03:00:23.120Z","stars":39,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["DFOS is an open protocol for identities, signed records, and delegated permissions that any compatible application can verify for itself.","Identity derives from Ed25519 signed operations, and an identifier derives from its genesis operation. Proofs verify offline, in any language, from any copy. Content chains reference documents by hash. The protocol does not encrypt, and whoever serves a document can read it. Which view of an identity you follow is a choice of relay.","This repository contains the protocol specification, reference implementations in TypeScript and Go, cross-language verification suites, and the CLI."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/metalabel/dfos/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"caa8c5e568f1fab81bb58051ffa83c5bf659d73f7c8199925b337ee478a2986d","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T02:48:13.752Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-17T03:00:23.265Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"DFOS is an open protocol for identities, signed records, and delegated permissions that any compatible application can verify for itself.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/metalabel/dfos/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account